I suspect the cause is that when the permission has already been granted, the `askForPermissions` call doesn’t return a response (i.e., it never resolves).

As a quick test, I ran the code below. The `status` remained `pending`, and it only changed to `granted` after I sent the app to the background once and then came back.

```tsx
  const [status, setStatus] = useState<'granted' | 'denied' | 'pending'>();
  const requestPermission = async () => {
    setStatus('pending');
    const result = await ImagePicker.requestCameraPermissionsAsync();
    setStatus(result.granted ? 'granted' : 'denied');
  }

  return (
    <View style={styles.container}>
      <Button title="Request Permission" onPress={requestPermission} />
      {status && <Text>{status}</Text>}
    </View>
  );

```

I observed the same behavior with `expo-camera`’s `useCameraPermissions` and with `expo-location`’s `useForegroundPermissions`.

> > In our case, we managed to kind of work around it by always calling `Location.getForegroundPermissionAsync` or `Location.getBackgroundPermissionAsync` before requesting it. Also, we'd check the `status` and `canAskAgain` values of the response and programatically direct the user to `AppSettings` if needed.
> 
> Thanks for the idea [@participant7](https://github.com/participant7) ! We found that `ImagePicker.requestCameraPermissionsAsync()` never returns in Android 16 (Expo SDK 52) so now instead of directly requesting permissions i first check if we already have them, with `ImagePicker.getCameraPermissionsAsync()`, and this workaround seems to work fine.

This was really helpful. We did this, but also added a delay for opening the camera if they chose take picture instead of choose from gallery:

```
  // Check and request camera permissions
  // First check current permission status (Android 16 workaround)
  let cameraPermissionResult = await ImagePicker.getCameraPermissionsAsync();

  // Only request permissions if we don't already have them
  if (!cameraPermissionResult.granted) {
    cameraPermissionResult = await ImagePicker.requestCameraPermissionsAsync();
  }
```
