How I understand the issue is that with the android update the permission state isn't resolving correctly. If you call launchCameraAsync, it is stuck getting permissions it already has. That's what the patch fixes. For now, that's fine until the update cycle of my team is updating to sdk54. Then we have to look, if the issue is resolved in some update of RN or the library itself.

